# Runtime origin — intentionally permissive policy (M2; ADR-0008).
# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages `_headers` format. GitHub Pages IGNORES this
# file (it cannot send custom headers) — the runtime page then ships with
# no CSP at all, which is the permissive baseline; the compensating
# controls are the separate origin, secret-free content, no service
# workers, no auth cookies, and the strict main-origin policy (see
# docs/architecture/deployment.md).
#
# The CSP below permits ordinary web dependencies for game HTML (inline
# scripts/modules, HTTPS scripts, HTTPS + WSS connections, remote
# images/fonts/audio/video/models, blob URLs) while still blocking object
# embedding and cross-origin framing of the runtime page.
#
# Substitute YOUR real origins before use:
#   - CSP `frame-ancestors` -> your main origin, e.g. https://nova.example
#     (the ONLY origin allowed to frame the runtime page; leave in place)
#   - Permissions-Policy `(self)` keeps camera/mic/clipboard delegation to
#     the game frame working (F4: delegation at every iframe hop).
# When the site uses a Vite base path (project-site layout), prefix the
# paths below with that base (e.g. /runtime/assets/*).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(self), clipboard-read=(self), clipboard-write=(self), fullscreen=(self)
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src * data: blob: 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval'; frame-ancestors https://nova.example; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
